# Long-form Novel Production

## Description: <br>
Create a continuous multi-chapter novel through a reusable directed lifecycle: establish the writing foundation, read accepted history and produce a recap, write or revise in one logical Writer session, run an independent review, and deliver accepted chapters. <br>

## Publisher: <br>
DevWerk <br>

## Category: <br>
creative_writing <br>

## Tags: <br>
- novel <br>
- long-form-writing <br>
- chapter-series <br>
- historical-recap <br>
- independent-review <br>
- directed-rework <br>

## Use Case: <br>
Use when the user needs a continuous chapter-based novel whose chapters must read prior accepted material, preserve auditable recaps, receive independent review, and return targeted feedback to the same Writer context. <br>

## Selection Guide: <br>
Select for a managed long-form fiction project with repeated chapter Tasks and explicit review/rework. Do not select for a short standalone passage, a single unreviewed response, or non-fiction software delivery. <br>

## Loop Input: <br>
Project title, confirmed premise, target chapter length, and permissive maximum chapter length. <br>

## Loop Output: <br>
Frozen writing guides, serial chapter summaries and bodies, review evidence, index, final acceptance evidence, and explicit Task terminal states. <br>

